wikipedia_extract: 'USS Tuscaloosa (CL/CA-37) was a New Orleans-class cruiser of the
  U.S. Navy. Commissioned in 1934, she spent most of her career in the Atlantic and
  Caribbean, participating in several European wartime operations. In early 1945,
  she transferred to the Pacific and assisted in shore bombardment of Iwo Jima and
  Okinawa. She earned 7 battle stars for her service in World War II. Never damaged
  in battle, the ship fared better compared to her six sister ships, three of which
  were sunk and the other three heavily damaged.

  Tuscaloosa was decommissioned in early 1946 and scrapped in 1959.'
